(7237789, 1118547, 156466, '<td valign="top">Great colors and lines.  Only critique is that you might want to do a touch of vertical perspective correction to get the vertical lines running parallel to the right edge (bump the bottom about +2 or 3).  Or is that the top?  Just noticed the perspective change.  Nicely done.</td>', 'Great colors and lines.  Only critique is that you might want to do a touch of vertical perspective correction to get the vertical lines running parallel to the right edge (bump the bottom about +2 or 3).  Or is that the top?  Just noticed the perspective change.  Nicely done.', '2014-07-07 10:03:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7237800, 1120687, 156466, '<td valign="top">Oh no - this just too darn lovely to have a horizon line like that!!  It''s not just a little crooked, it''s a LOT crooked.  Even if that''s the way it is in reality (which I don''t think it is since the verticals in the reflection line up perfectly when I straighten the horizon), it throws the photo off - at least for this person.  Would have been in my top three easily, but I can''t.  9 or 10 is a generous 7.  Everything else is stunning, but you missed that one critical detail.</td>', 'Oh no - this just too darn lovely to have a horizon line like that!!  It''s not just a little crooked, it''s a LOT crooked.  Even if that''s the way it is in reality (which I don''t think it is since the verticals in the reflection line up perfectly when I straighten the horizon), it throws the photo off - at least for this person.  Would have been in my top three easily, but I can''t.  9 or 10 is a generous 7.  Everything else is stunning, but you missed that one critical detail.', '2014-07-07 10:08:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(7237809, 1120553, 156466, '<td valign="top">Very cool treatment and photo that loses a point for leaning a hair too far to the right - which has nothing to do with the fisheye/ultrawide distortion that I love. Still an 8.</td>', 'Very cool treatment and photo that loses a point for leaning a hair too far to the right - which has nothing to do with the fisheye/ultrawide distortion that I love. Still an 8.', '2014-07-07 10:12:18.000000', NULL, 1),
